  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is on. I also couldn't call the plan-approval tool, since it isn't available in this session. Please confirm the plan below and I'll apply it.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment character by default. Everything from an unquoted `#` onward is dropped, so `prog a#b` becomes `[\"prog\", \"a\"]`. Completion then runs on a truncated word list.\n\n**Fix:** Add `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True`.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- Add tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, such as `\"prog a#b\"` giving `[\"prog\", \"a#b\"]`.\n- Add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-golden-treasure.md`.",
